PART 2 - AUTHENTICATION: USER LOGIN vs ADMIN LOGIN (REAL, SERVER-SIDE)
=====================================================================
Requirements
2.1 Passwords: hash with crypto.scrypt (N=2^15 or higher, random 16-byte salt,
    stored as "scrypt$N$r$p$salt$hash"), constant-time compare with
    timingSafeEqual. Min length 10, block the top common passwords list
    (include a small bundled list). Never log passwords or tokens.
2.2 Sessions: random 256-bit token -> cookie `sid` (httpOnly, SameSite=Lax,
    Secure when HTTPS or NODE_ENV=production, Path=/, 7-day sliding expiry
    for users, 60-minute idle expiry for admins). Store only SHA-256(token)
    in the DB. Logout deletes the row. Rotate session id on login and on role
    or password change.
2.3 CSRF: for POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE require a custom header
    `X-Requested-With: fetch` AND verify the Origin/Host match the server's
    allowed origins.
2.4 Brute force: max 5 failed logins per email+IP per 15 minutes then
    lock 15 minutes (increment failed_logins, set locked_until). Generic
    error text ("Invalid email or password") - never reveal which one.
2.5 Two DIFFERENT login surfaces:
    - USER: routes /login, /register, /forgot (for a local app, implement
      "reset by admin" instead of email: admin generates a one-time
      temporary password with must_change_pw=true). Role 'user' only.
    - ADMIN: separate route /admin/login with its own page and styling
      ("Administrator sign-in"). It accepts ONLY role='admin'. A normal user
      typing correct user credentials there must get the same generic
      failure. Admin and user sessions are distinct (admin session has
      shorter idle time and requires re-auth to change keys or delete users).
2.6 First admin bootstrap: read ADMIN_EMAIL and ADMIN_PASSWORD from the
    environment on first boot ONLY when no admin exists. If they are missing,
    generate a random 20-char password, print it ONCE to the server console
    with a warning, and set must_change_pw=true. There must be NO hardcoded
    default credential anywhere (remove 'admin123' from AdminModal.jsx, the
    README and every test).
2.7 RBAC middleware: requireAuth, requireRole('admin'). Every route and every
    WebSocket message type gets an explicit access rule in one table
    (server/auth/policy.mjs). Default = deny. User endpoints always filter by
    session.user_id (row-level ownership): a user can never read, edit or
    delete another user's trip (return 404, not 403, to avoid enumeration).
2.8 WebSocket: on upgrade verify (a) cookie session valid, (b) Origin is in
    the allowlist (localhost:PORT, 127.0.0.1:PORT, Vite dev port, and any
    origins in ALLOWED_ORIGINS env). Reject with 401/403 otherwise. Attach
    user {id, role} to the socket. Messages starting with `admin_` require
    role==='admin' re-checked per message. `chat`/`stop`/`reset` require any
    authenticated user and operate only on that user's trip. Cap message size
    (e.g. 256 KB) and rate-limit per socket.
2.9 Remove the /debug/tool route in production. In dev only, require admin
    session AND NODE_ENV!=='production'.
2.10 Remove `localStorage 'ulisse_admin_auth'` entirely. The frontend learns
    the role from GET /api/me only.

Admin capabilities (admin dashboard, route /admin, role-guarded)
  - Overview: user count, trips count, active sessions, server health, data
    source status (Nominatim/Overpass/Wikipedia/OSRM/Open-Meteo reachable?
    last success time), cache hit rate.
  - Users: list, search, disable/enable, force password reset, change role,
    delete (with confirm + re-auth). An admin cannot demote/delete the last
    remaining admin or themselves.
  - Trips (privacy-safe): metadata only (owner, destination, dates,
    created_at, size). Admin does NOT read the contents of a user's trip
    unless an explicit "support access" toggle is enabled in settings; when
    used it is written to the audit log.
  - API keys / engine config (Gemini, Groq, OpenAI-compatible, optional
    places/pricing keys): stored ENCRYPTED at rest (AES-256-GCM, key from
    ENCRYPTION_KEY env; refuse to start in production if missing). The API
    only ever returns a masked preview (last 4 chars). Never send full keys
    to the browser.
  - Audit log viewer (filter by actor/action/date) and CSV export.
  - Maintenance: clear places cache, refresh FX rates now, run data-source
    health check.
Normal user features: register/login/logout, edit profile (display name, home
currency, language), change password, own trips CRUD, export/import own trips
as JSON, delete own account (with password confirmation).

Auth tests (vitest + a test HTTP client; must be in CI)
  - scrypt hash/verify round trip; wrong password fails; timing-safe path
  - lockout after 5 failures; generic error message
  - session expiry, logout invalidation, session rotation
  - user cannot open /admin/* or call admin_* WS messages (403)
  - user A cannot GET/PUT/DELETE user B's trip (404)
  - WS upgrade with Origin https://evil.example is rejected
  - WS upgrade without cookie is rejected
  - last-admin protection; no default credentials present in the repo
