PART 3 - SERVER HARDENING
=====================================================================
3.1 Security headers on every response: Content-Security-Policy (default-src
    'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://*.tile.openstreetmap.org and any
    provider image hosts actually used; connect-src 'self' ws: wss: plus the
    public APIs the BROWSER calls directly, if any), X-Content-Type-Options:
    nosniff, Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin,
    X-Frame-Options: DENY (the promo-site demo iframe lives on another
    build and is unaffected), Permissions-Policy minimal.
3.2 Static file server: resolve with path.resolve and verify the result
    startsWith(DIST) before reading; unknown paths -> SPA fallback only for
    GET requests that accept text/html, otherwise 404 JSON.
3.3 JSON body limit (1 MB, 413 on excess), content-type check, Zod schema
    validation for EVERY API input (extend the existing zod usage). Validate
    trip data on load and import (TripSchema mirroring normalizeTrip in
    src/lib/utils.js); return a clear 422 with field errors - never crash or
    silently repair.
3.4 Rate limiting: per IP for /api/auth/* (strict), /api/places/* (respect
    upstream limits), and chat messages per user per minute.
3.5 Central error handler: log detail server-side with a request id, return
    a generic message + request id to the client.
3.6 Docker: run as non-root user, add HEALTHCHECK on /health, keep
    AGENT_HOST=0.0.0.0 only in Docker, and make docker-compose require
    SESSION_SECRET, ENCRYPTION_KEY, ADMIN_EMAIL, ADMIN_PASSWORD (fail fast
    with a clear message if unset). Update .env.example with every variable.
3.7 Remove the Booking.com / Google Maps headless-Chrome scraping from the
    default path (see PART 4). If you keep the code, gate it behind
    ULISSE_ENABLE_SCRAPERS=1, default OFF, with a comment that it may
    violate the sites' Terms of Service and is unsupported.

